What is Sodium Cyanide?
Sodium Cyanide (NaCN) is a highly toxic, white, water-soluble inorganic compound. Its defining chemical characteristic is a strong affinity for metals, which underpins its significant commercial value. The compound is classified as a basic chemical raw material and requires extreme caution in handling, as contact with acids can release hydrogen cyanide, a lethal gas. Its high toxicity necessitates rigorous safety protocols throughout its lifecycle, from production and transportation to its end-use application and waste management.
